x86/microcode: Add explicit CPU vendor dependency

jira KERNEL-814
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-4.18.0-553.115.1.el8_10
commit-author Borislav Petkov <bp@suse.de>
commit 9c55d99e099bd7aa6b91fce8718505c35d5dfc65
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-4.18.0-553.115.1.el8_10/9c55d99e.failed

Add an explicit dependency to the respective CPU vendor so that the
respective microcode support for it gets built only when that support is
enabled.

	Reported-by: Randy Dunlap <rdunlap@infradead.org>
	Signed-off-by: Borislav Petkov <bp@suse.de>
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/8ead0da9-9545-b10d-e3db-7df1a1f219e4@infradead.org
(cherry picked from commit 9c55d99e099bd7aa6b91fce8718505c35d5dfc65)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

# Conflicts:
#	arch/x86/Kconfig
diff --cc arch/x86/Kconfig
index af1b96027394,7ba627c60504..000000000000
--- a/arch/x86/Kconfig
+++ b/arch/x86/Kconfig
@@@ -1340,9 -1313,9 +1340,9 @@@ config MICROCOD
  
  config MICROCODE_INTEL
  	bool "Intel microcode loading support"
- 	depends on MICROCODE
+ 	depends on CPU_SUP_INTEL && MICROCODE
  	default MICROCODE
 -	help
 +	---help---
  	  This options enables microcode patch loading support for Intel
  	  processors.
  
@@@ -1352,8 -1325,8 +1352,13 @@@
  
  config MICROCODE_AMD
  	bool "AMD microcode loading support"
++<<<<<<< HEAD
 +	depends on MICROCODE
 +	---help---
++=======
+ 	depends on CPU_SUP_AMD && MICROCODE
+ 	help
++>>>>>>> 9c55d99e099b (x86/microcode: Add explicit CPU vendor dependency)
